---
import WorksheetLayout from '../../../../layouts/WorksheetLayout.astro';
---
<WorksheetLayout
  title="Design Notes"
  lesson="/courses/mfedu-2026/sketch-to-story/"
  intro="Ideas first, neatness never. Use this page to think — fragments, arrows, and doodles all count."
>
  <h2>The story in one sentence</h2>
  <div class="ws-lines"><div></div><div></div></div>

  <h2>Ideas — all of them</h2>
  <p>Sketch or list every version you can think of. Quantity beats quality here; you'll choose later.</p>
  <div class="ws-box ws-box--tall"></div>

  <h2>Reality check</h2>
  <div class="ws-grid">
    <div>
      <p><strong>Materials I actually have:</strong></p>
      <div class="ws-lines"><div></div><div></div><div></div></div>
    </div>
    <div>
      <p><strong>Skills I need to learn:</strong></p>
      <div class="ws-lines"><div></div><div></div><div></div></div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <h2>The one I'm building</h2>
  <p>Final sketch — front view. Mark where the circuit lives: battery, lights, and switch.</p>
  <div class="ws-box ws-box--tall"></div>

  <h2>First three steps</h2>
  <div class="ws-lines"><div></div><div></div><div></div></div>
  <p class="ws-hint">A plan that fits in three steps actually gets started.</p>
</WorksheetLayout>
